{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 900 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "78612288ded088d6976fa417d6722729f070ac71c23f7894447c98f37856e26d" :edb/db-before-t 899 :edb/db-after-t 900 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534212 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:47:42.565Z" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186147497 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414153 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186148223 1068 #edb/ref 17592186147092 13194139534212 17592186045417 false] [17592186148223 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414152 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186148223 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186148223 1071 "![](images/93/936d303dcc89c5c27e77fa3d7cfc8b63643284d9e203f176c9e0c5588c27e049.png)\n\nConsiderer the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=1$ is a node.\n- $y=-2$ is a sink.\n- $y=3$ is a source." 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186148223 1071 "![](images/93/936d303dcc89c5c27e77fa3d7cfc8b63643284d9e203f176c9e0c5588c27e049.png)\n\nConsiderer the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $y = 1$ is a node.\n2. $y =-2$ is a sink.\n3. $y = 3$ is a source." 13194139534212 17592186045417 false] [17592186148223 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/69/69e895d4091075f6d50eb9e44dc027c342d1fe7ca0269224c9b6a019ab312c77.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=3$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414154 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414155 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414156 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414157 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414158 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1045 "Classifying Equilibrium Solutions of First-Order ODEs" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1046 #edb/ref 17592186414157 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048131 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414140 1053 #uuid "8f67b1d8-cc12-5be2-bedd-7d8ea39d1438" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414141 1080 "images/b5/b5e7a0272bb45b9d83ec8864f58cf3b96cbb6399d079f23d168d8de5416a1c23.png" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414141 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414141 1083 #uuid "1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414142 1080 "images/8d/8d608e5ab231af991d4c55ca863e95557faae55bf44ad0e8e99f7cd0417531f2.png" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414142 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414142 1083 #uuid "5bd318dd-9201-58a9-b18d-379eb2818d97" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [175921864