on has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a sink\n\n- $y=0$ is a source\n\n- $y=3$ is a sink\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414153 1072 #uuid "57d5be79-8453-52cc-b08d-ee25cf4792e4" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414153 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-3,$ $y=0,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=0$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-2$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n![](images/a4/a4d0e0f44f77e0d29d6d226b058806e947b38f4784dc61ea609ac1040b73d7dd.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/b5/b5e7a0272bb45b9d83ec8864f58cf3b96cbb6399d079f23d168d8de5416a1c23.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-3,$ $y=0,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-3$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=0$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to converge toward this line." 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414154 1062 #uuid "4301353b-f307-5ad7-9fa6-573ee6bd3b91" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414154 1063 #edb/ref 17592186314831 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414155 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414154 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414155 1062 #uuid "4bcfd21f-7077-56a5-b180-c56af3baefcb" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414155 1063 #edb/ref 17592186414153 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414156 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414158 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414156 1062 #uuid "4cca875a-cd23-5293-b9eb-53796fc6ca53" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414156 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362326 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414157 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414156 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414157 1062 #uuid "d28d673b-fc35-5482-abfa-3f1e7616614a" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414157 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148223 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414158 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414155 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414158 1062 #uuid "dc1c1dd6-77b7-596c-aadc-9bd547e58f0f" 13194139534212 17592186045417 true] [17592186414158 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362330 13194139534212 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-8f67b1d8-cc12-5be2-bedd-7d8ea39d1438" 17592186414140 "answer-1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406" 17592186414141 "answer-5bd318dd-9201-58a9-b18d-379eb2818d97" 17592186414142 "answer-61206ccb-548f-5100-91ee-609c064a5202" 17592186414143 "answer-69c30199-4328-5a15-bfcf-b46f5467a96f" 17592186414144 "answer-6a4eb0a3-0396-53b2-9786-1fe15d9dc42d" 17592186414145 "answer-80ba1f07-d31e-5ece-ad1d-7de624148041" 17592186414146 "answer-9cf91e35-e89f-544d-aac8-8bed29bb7a2b" 17592186414147 "answer-b82bf18a-7b1c-5303-9140-3233520ff812" 1759218641414